Reading: localization.md

Use ARB-backed copy and bind localizations once at the top of `build`:

```dart
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final l10n = context.l10n;

  return Scaffold(
    appBar: AppBar(
      title: Text(l10n.settingsTitle),
    ),
    body: ...
    // wherever the save action is rendered
    child: Text(l10n.saveButton),
  );
}
```

Fixes:
- `Text('Save')` -> `Text(l10n.saveButton)`
- `Text('Settings')` -> `Text(l10n.settingsTitle)`
- `SettingsStrings.title` -> do not use it for visible copy; keep `SettingsStrings` only for non-user-facing IDs, or remove it if it exists just for UI text
- `context.l10n.saveButton` chained directly in `build` -> bind `final l10n = context.l10n;` once, then use `l10n.saveButton`

Add the title key to ARB if it does not already exist:

```json
{
  "settingsTitle": "Settings",
  "@settingsTitle": {
    "description": "Title shown on the settings screen"
  }
}
```

If `saveButton` already exists, reuse it as-is.

